From 5b526e14ffedcee54b59b6822c6788522ffa5064 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mabn <github@mabn.pl>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:51:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 133/149] [barreplay] P12: the synced projectile collision pass
 with its detections run on all threads first (toggle3 0x2)

A projectile whose detection found nothing to act on (no shield it would
reach, no unit or feature it would hit) is skipped in the pass, drawing the
synced tempNum its query would have, when nothing it read can have changed:
the pass's effects mark the cells (256 elmos) of what they touch - a damaged
or killed unit and its shields, an added or removed feature, a shield taking
a projectile - and a Lua write other than rules params and team resources, a
unit or shield changing quads, or a transport dying marks everything. The
projectile's own position, speed and radius must be unchanged too. Every
other projectile runs the ordinary code. From 256 projectiles
(BARREPLAY_P12_MINPROJ); BARREPLAY_P12_CHECK runs the ordinary code for every
would-be skip and counts the ones that acted (wrong= on the bench line).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
